    "updated_at": "2020-11-04T03:03:57Z",
    "body": "I faced this problem too. I am on:\r\n\r\n    Starship version: 0.46.2\r\n    zsh version: zsh 5.4.2 (x86_64-ubuntu-linux-gnu)\r\n    Operating system: elementaryOS Hera 5.1.7 (Based off Ubuntu 18.04)\r\n    Terminal emulator: hyper 3.0.2\r\n\r\nIt was a fresh install of zsh and starship. The only packages I had were `zsh-vim-mode` and `zsh-syntax-highlighting`. By troubleshooting every single aspect of the build, I found that the broken hole was `zsh-vim-mode`. If you have it, try to not include it and source `.zshrc` again to see if it fixes the problem.\r\n\r\nI would also like to note that I do not think that `zsh-vim-mode` is the key problem, seeing how it works perfectly fine with all my other machines with oh-my-zsh/spaceship-prompt.",
