    "body": "This just started happening to me as well. It didn't happen yesterday, I haven't changed anything 😕 \r\n\r\nNow, any time I enter command mode *and* enter insert mode, a couple of lines above the cursor is eaten up.\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/597206/107743660-94029180-6d11-11eb-8c31-d2eb98fb33b6.mov\r\n\r\nThis is *extremely* annoying. Any luck figuring out what the cause of this is?\r\n\r\n```\r\n- Starship version: 0.50.0\r\n- zsh version: zsh 5.8 (x86_64-apple-darwin20.0)\r\n- Operating system: macOS Big Sur 11.2 (20D64)\r\n- Terminal emulator: Terminal and iTerm2\r\n```\r\n\r\nEDIT: Just to clarify, this only happens to me on macOS. On Linux, this only happens when I press Esc twice while in `history-incremental-search-backward` mode, as described in my bug report above.",
